BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[Killarney] Planned Outage - Arrêt planifié
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260609T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260611T000000
DTSTAMP:20260703T134918Z
UID:drac-incident-1617@status.alliancecan.ca
CATEGORIES:SCHEDULED
DESCRIPTION:On Tuesday and Wednesday\, June 9-10 \, 2026 Vector's Killarn
 ey high performance computing grid will be shut down as U of T/SciNet will
  be performing data centre-wide maintenance upgrades to the environmental 
 and electrical systems.\nDuring this period users will be unable to login 
 . HPC compute nodes in the cluster will be shut down and queued jobs will 
 not execute. Running jobs will be cancelled.\nThe Scientific Computing tea
 m will take advantage of these maintenance windows to perform upgrades to 
 address security\, performance and add enhancements to the environment.\n\
 nhttps://status.alliancecan.ca/view_incident?incident=1617
URL:https://status.alliancecan.ca/view_incident?incident=1617
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[Trillium] Planned Outage - Arrêt planifié
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260609T040000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260611T000000
DTSTAMP:20260703T134918Z
UID:drac-incident-1629@status.alliancecan.ca
CATEGORIES:SCHEDULED
DESCRIPTION:As part of the installation of the AI expansion for the Trill
 ium cluster\, t he next maintenance window is scheduled for June 9-10\, be
 ginning at 4:00 AM EDT.\nDuring this period\, most systems located in the 
 SciNet datacentre will be down.  This includes HPSS\, Open OnDemand\, S4H
 \, Balam\, Teach\, Neptune\, Killarney and the other Vector Institute syst
 ems.  The Trillium login nodes and storage will remain up and available.
   The Trillium and Trillium-GPU compute nodes will be down initially\, an
 d we will power them up gradually as cooling permits.\n\nhttps://status.al
 liancecan.ca/view_incident?incident=1629
URL:https://status.alliancecan.ca/view_incident?incident=1629
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[Killarney] Planned Outage - Arrêt planifié
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260622T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260627T000000
DTSTAMP:20260703T134918Z
UID:drac-incident-1618@status.alliancecan.ca
CATEGORIES:SCHEDULED
DESCRIPTION:On Monday to Friday\, June 22-26 \, 2026 Vector's Killarney h
 igh performance computing grid will be shut down as U of T/SciNet will be 
 performing data centre-wide maintenance upgrades to the environmental and 
 electrical systems. A power down of the equipment will begin June 21\, 20:
 00 ET .\nDuring this period users will be unable to login . HPC compute no
 des in all clusters will be shut down and queued jobs will not execute. Ru
 nning jobs will be cancelled.\nThe Scientific Computing team will take adv
 antage of these maintenance windows to perform upgrades to address securit
 y\, performance and add enhancements to the environment.\n\nhttps://status
 .alliancecan.ca/view_incident?incident=1618
URL:https://status.alliancecan.ca/view_incident?incident=1618
END:VEVENT
